{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Avram passed through the land.</b> He entered into it." "<b>As far as the site of Shechem.</b> To pray for the sons of Jacob, when they would come to fight against Shechem." "<b>The plain of Moreh.</b> That is Shechem. He showed him Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal, where Israel accepted the oath of the Torah." "<b>And the Canaanite was then in the land.</b> He was going and conquering the land of Israel from the seed of Shem, for in the portion of Shem it had fallen when Noah divided the land among his sons, as it says ״וּמַלְכִּי צֶדֶק מֶלֶךְ שָׁלֵם״ (Genesis 14). Therefore ״וַיֹּאמֶר YHWH אֶל אַבְרָם לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת״ — I am destined to return it to your children, for they are of the seed of Shem."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:24.379965484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}